From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:22:13 +0000
Subject: [debug][wasm] Defer debugger break in optimized Wasm frames
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Debug::HandleDebugBreak deoptimizes the top JavaScript frame before it
enters the debugger. However, Deoptimizer::DeoptimizeFunction skips
WebAssembly frames. If an interrupt triggers Debug::HandleDebugBreak
inside a Turboshaft WebAssembly frame, the frame stays optimized on the
stack. While the debugger pauses the program, JavaScript can modify
WebAssembly tables or state. These changes break compiler assumptions
in the active Turboshaft frame.

To prevent this bug, Debug::HandleDebugBreak now checks the top
debuggable frame. If the frame is a non-Liftoff WebAssembly frame, the
debugger defers the break. It calls SetBreakOnNextFunctionCall and
returns immediately. This patch also updates DebugInfoImpl::IsStepping
and ExecuteWasmDebugBreaks to check scheduled_break_on_function_call.
A deferred break now pauses at the entry of the next JS or Liftoff
WebAssembly function.

(cherry picked from commit afd4fd529a4bf40bd832fc525802c40d049cedad)

